<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James VI and I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1566–1625</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as James VI of Scotland, James I of England</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James VI and I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> as James VI from 1567 and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Ireland as James I from 1603 until his death in 1625. The son of Mary, Queen of Scots, he inherited the English crown on the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>, joining the crowns of the two kingdoms in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-the-crowns">Union of the Crowns</a>, though they kept separate parliaments. He sponsored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-james-version">King James Bible</a> of 1611.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i.jpg" alt="James VI and I" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to John de Critz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JamesIEngland_(cropped_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
